# create_anim_blueprint_sample Design

Date: 2026-06-27

Status: Implemented first pass on 2026-06-27.

Scope: editor-only, sample-only Animation Blueprint creation from a Skeleton or
SkeletalMesh. Runtime/gameplay code and original asset mutation are out of
scope.

## Purpose

`create_anim_blueprint_sample` is a narrow UnrealMCP bridge command
for creating a sample AnimBP under `/Game/_MCP_Sample/` or `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`
when a later sample command needs an AnimBP target but the user has only
provided a Skeleton or SkeletalMesh.

The command should:

- validate the Skeleton or derive it from a SkeletalMesh;
- create a `UAnimBlueprint` using `UAnimBlueprintFactory`;
- set a preview SkeletalMesh when available;
- use a bounded parent class, defaulting to `UAnimInstance`;
- compile, optionally save, and return readback evidence.

The command exists because generic Blueprint creation is not enough for AnimBP
work. AnimBPs need a target skeleton, AnimInstance parent class, preview mesh,
and compile/readback handling.

## Ieta Review

Request class: create a safe sample Animation Blueprint from a Skeleton or
SkeletalMesh as setup for state-machine, ControlRig-node, Post Process, or
node-attribution work.

Existing routes checked:

- Generic Blueprint creation can create ordinary Blueprint assets but does not
  validate AnimBP-specific skeleton and preview mesh requirements.
- Existing sample AnimGraph commands can edit or duplicate sample AnimBPs once
  a suitable AnimBP exists.
- `set_skeletal_mesh_component_anim_defaults` assigns an AnimBP class to a
  component template but does not create the AnimBP asset.

Why existing routes are insufficient: they do not expose a narrow AnimBP
factory wrapper with skeleton validation and sample-root guards.

Asset mutation boundary: input Skeleton and SkeletalMesh are read-only. The
command may create or modify only the target AnimBP under `/Game/_MCP_Sample/`
or `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`.

Implemented command: `create_anim_blueprint_sample`.

Default safety guard: require target path under sample/temp roots, require
either a Skeleton or a SkeletalMesh, reject overwrite unless explicitly allowed,
and reject final/original project asset creation.

Approval status: user approved Ieta/Tivret continuation on 2026-06-27. First
implementation remains editor-only, sample-only, and runtime-code-free.

## UE 5.6 API Anchors

Use installed UE 5.6 headers as local truth:

| Need | UE 5.6 anchor | Safe access rule |
| --- | --- | --- |
| AnimBP factory | `Engine/Source/Editor/UnrealEd/Classes/Factories/AnimBlueprintFactory.h` | Configure `BlueprintType`, `ParentClass`, `TargetSkeleton`, `PreviewSkeletalMesh`, and `bTemplate=false`. |
| AnimBP asset | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/AnimBlueprint.h` | Return generated class through AnimBP APIs after compile rather than Python `generated_class` guesses. |
| AnimInstance parent | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/AnimInstance.h` | Default parent must be `UAnimInstance` or a subclass. |
| Skeleton | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/Animation/Skeleton.h` | Use explicit Skeleton path or derive from SkeletalMesh. |
| SkeletalMesh | `Engine/Source/Runtime/Engine/Classes/Engine/SkeletalMesh.h` | Use as read-only source for Skeleton and preview mesh. |
| Asset creation | `AssetToolsModule`, `Factories/Factory.h` | Create asset through the factory path, not by constructing packages manually. |
| Blueprint compile | `Kismet2/KismetEditorUtilities.h` | Compile after creation and return warnings/errors. |

## Command Schema

Proposed input fields:

| Field | Type | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `target_anim_bp_path` | string | required | Must be under `/Game/_MCP_Sample/` or `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`. |
| `skeleton_path` | string | optional | Explicit target Skeleton. Required when no mesh is supplied. |
| `skeletal_mesh_path` | string | optional | Read-only mesh used to derive Skeleton and preview mesh. |
| `preview_skeletal_mesh_path` | string | optional | Overrides mesh preview source when supplied. |
| `parent_class_path` | string | `/Script/Engine.AnimInstance` | Must resolve to `UAnimInstance` subclass. |
| `overwrite_existing` | bool | `false` | Reject existing target by default. |
| `compile` | bool | `true` | Compile after creation. |
| `save_asset` | bool | `false` | Save only the target sample asset. |
| `dry_run` | bool | `false` | Resolve assets and planned action without mutation. |

At least one of `skeleton_path` or `skeletal_mesh_path` is required. If both
are supplied, validate that the mesh uses the same Skeleton unless an explicit
future option allows mismatch handling.

## Response Schema

Return structured evidence:

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `success` | Whether creation completed. |
| `dry_run` | Whether mutation was skipped. |
| `target_anim_bp_path` | Created or planned sample AnimBP path. |
| `skeleton_path` | Resolved Skeleton path. |
| `skeletal_mesh_path` | Input mesh path when supplied. |
| `preview_skeletal_mesh_path` | Preview mesh applied or planned. |
| `parent_class_path` | Resolved AnimInstance parent class. |
| `created` | True when a new asset was created. |
| `overwrote_existing` | True only when explicitly allowed. |
| `generated_class_path` | Generated class path after compile when available. |
| `compile_result` | Compile status, warnings, and errors. |
| `compile_succeeded` / `save_succeeded` | Final requested compile/save outcome. Top-level `success` must be false when a requested compile or save fails. |
| `completion_errors` | Failure tokens such as `compile_failed` or `save_failed` when finalization did not complete. |
| `source_modified` | Must be false for Skeleton and SkeletalMesh inputs. |
| `warnings` | Validation warnings or skipped optional work. |

## Guardrails

Forbidden patterns:

- creating assets outside `/Game/_MCP_Sample/` or `/Game/_MCP_Temp/`;
- overwriting an existing target without `overwrite_existing=true`;
- modifying Skeleton, SkeletalMesh, or any original project AnimBP;
- creating runtime/gameplay classes or adding project module dependencies;
- using a non-AnimInstance parent class;
- treating a generic Blueprint as an AnimBP;
- using Python `generated_class` access as the success proof.

The first implementation should create an empty/default AnimBP only. It should
not also author state machines, ControlRig nodes, or graph demos; those belong
to separate sample commands.

## Verification

Docs-only verification for this design:

- `git diff --check`
- Markdown link and trailing-whitespace sanity checks.

Implementation verification:

1. `dry_run=true` validates Skeleton or SkeletalMesh without dirtying packages.
2. Create a target under `/Game/_MCP_Sample/` and compile.
3. Confirm generated class is a `UAnimBlueprintGeneratedClass`.
4. Read back target Skeleton and preview mesh.
5. Confirm input Skeleton and SkeletalMesh packages are not dirty.
6. Re-run with existing target and `overwrite_existing=false`; expect a
   structured `target_exists` error.
7. Reject a target path outside sample/temp roots.

## Tivret Maintenance Notes

When maintaining this command, Tivret should:

- implement the factory wrapper as the smallest editor-only command possible;
- keep graph authoring out of this command;
- add Python wrapper and server registration only after the C++ response schema
  is stable;
- document the command near the animation/controlrig tool docs;
- avoid runtime modules, gameplay dependencies, asset assignment to live
  components, or original asset mutation;
- verify dry-run, create, compile/readback, existing-target rejection, and
  no-dirty-source behavior.
